  "prompt": "Compare two scenarios of SCOUT's Quad Cities flood projection, as SCOUT's own flood example does: one with no nature-based solutions in place, and a copy of it with all four (one per kind of solution). A shared setting holds the projection period, 2020 to 2050; the projection covers SCOUT's whole flood grid, as SCOUT's example does. In each scenario, run SCOUT's flood projection with that scenario's solutions, which gives the flood depth and SCOUT's own metrics; take the depth and draw it on its own Autark map in blues, and take SCOUT's metrics, whose median flood depth the comparison shows. Then take the absolute difference of the two scenarios' depths, cell by cell, with a raster calculator, and draw it on an Autark map in blues; and compare the two scenarios' median and mean flood depth in one Vega-Lite table that compares the scenarios: one row per scenario, its values in its scenario's colour, one column per metric. SCOUT's flood projection is not part of the standard node set, so whatever provides it needs installing first.",
