  "notes": "Two scenarios over a shared context: one Parameter node (the period; the region is SCOUT's whole grid, in the package's code), and in each scenario SCOUT's Flood Projection with its solutions, returning the depth and SCOUT's metrics, a node taking the depth for an Autark map, and one taking SCOUT's metrics. A Python node takes the absolute difference of the two depths (curio_raster_calculate(\"subtract\", [input_1, input_0], absolute=True)) and an Autark node maps it, and a Vega-Lite table comparing the scenarios (its spec reads its inputs stacked, the dataset inputs, and names each circle's scenario from __input__) shows SCOUT's median and mean flood depth from its stacked inputs, one row per scenario."
